Decision and sequencing: Comparison lane after initial content/metadata changes. Decision: measure embedded-entry marginal contribution by recompressing the original decompressed body with versus without that ZIP entry, preserving unrelated bytes; disclose non-additivity, compression context, and unavailable estimates rather than label ZIP length as outer contribution.

Refined ownership decision after exploration: isolated measurement helper and dedicated tests may proceed in parallel in their own worktree; reserve DiffMode/DiffData/JSON/renderer integration until the active comparison and renderer slices land. Measure matched recompression baseline versus removal trial, preserve original-body bytes outside ZIP span and embedded identities/textures. Negative/non-additive results are valid; baseline resave alone is not savings.